# vercel.json builds web/ and serves web/out, so nothing outside web/ is served.
# Without this every deploy uploads the whole parquet corpus, about 15 MB, to be
# ignored. vercel.json itself must stay: Vercel reads it.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. These follow .gitignore
# semantics, so a bare `data` matches ANY directory named data at any depth,
# which silently excluded web/public/data and failed the build with
# "Can't resolve '@/public/data/access.json'".
/data
/src
/tests
/scripts
/memory
/docs
/.github
/.claude
/*.md
/jd.txt
/NOTICE
/requirements.txt
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
